<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Butana</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Island of Meroë</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Butana is a semi-arid plain in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>, the Atbara and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blue-nile">Blue Nile</a>, known in antiquity as the Island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meroe">Meroë</a>. It was the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kushite kingdom</a> of Meroë, with sites such as Naqa and Musawwarat es-Sufra, and later lay within the Christian kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alodia">Alodia</a>. It remains important grazing land for pastoral peoples.</p></div>
